body:
If you delete the resource while the scene with the panel is open "copy" of the deleted StyleBox will be kept in the panel. It stays there even after closing and opening godot again and can be safely removed or saved into the filesystem

If its deleted when the panel's scene is closed a reference to the delete StyleBox is still alive and the engine crashes.
I see 2 solutions:
- Before calling the draw method check if the panel_style is null , if its null get a fallback style
``` .cpp
case NOTIFICATION_DRAW: {
	RID ci = get_canvas_item();
	Ref<StyleBox> style = theme_cache.panel_style;
	// If assigned style is deleted, get a default style
	if (style.is_null()) {
		style = ThemeDB::get_singleton()->get_fallback_stylebox();
	}
	style->draw(ci, Rect2(Point2(), get_size()));
} break;
```
- Or reproduce the same behavior when the scene is closed: clean the resource reference and keep a valid copy there. Which i think is related to this MissingResource
``` .cpp
if (ResourceLoader::is_creating_missing_resources_if_class_unavailable_enabled()) {
	missing_resource = memnew(MissingResource);
	missing_resource->set_original_class(res_type);
	missing_resource->set_recording_properties(true);
	obj = missing_resource;
```
